       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the usual maximum for metformin. The labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, usually given as 850 mg three times daily or 1,000 mg twice daily. A 1,700 mg single dose is also well above the usual per-dose range. At this level, the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity is high, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nCould this be a typo? Some possibilities:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day)\n- **1,000 mg twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **1,700 mg total per day**, divided into two doses (for example 850 mg twice daily)\n\nTell me the dose you intended and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that it's deliberate and give the clinical reason. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy before I enter it."
      }
